\begin{enumerate}
\item
  \textbf{Question}\\
  Seja \(X\) uma variável aleatória contínua com função de densidade:
  \[f_X(x) = \left\{
      \begin{array}{ll}
      \theta x^{\theta-1}, & \mbox{se}\, \ \ 0 \leq x \leq 1; \\ 
      0, & \text{caso contrário}.\\
      \end{array}
      \right. \nonumber\] Qual é a variância de \(X\), se \(\theta=4\)?

  \begin{enumerate}
  \def\labelenumii{(\alph{enumii})}
  \item
    \(0.67\)
  \item
    \(1.31\)
  \item
    \(0.24\)
  \item
    \(0.03\)
  \item
    \(0.64\)
  \end{enumerate}

  \textbf{Solution}\\
  \[\begin{aligned}
  E(X) & = \int_{-\infty}^{\infty} x f(x) dx \\
  & = \int_{0}^{1} x\theta x^{\theta -1} dx \\
  & = \theta\int_{0}^{1} x^{\theta} dx \\
  & = \frac{\theta}{\theta+1}\left[x^{\theta+1}\right]_{0}^{1} \\
  & = \frac{\theta}{\theta+1} = 0.8 .
  \end{aligned}\]

  \[\begin{aligned}
  E(X^2) & = \int_{-\infty}^{\infty} x^2 f(x) dx \\
  & = \int_{0}^{1} x^{2}\theta x^{\theta -1} dx \\
  & = \theta\int_{0}^{1} x^{\theta+1} dx \\
  & = \frac{\theta}{\theta+2}\left[x^{\theta+2}\right]_{0}^{1} \\
  & = \frac{\theta}{\theta+2} = 0.67 .
  \end{aligned}\]

  Portanto,
  \[Var(X)=E(X^{2})-\left[E(x)\right]^{2}=\frac{\theta}{\theta+2} - \frac{\theta^2}{(\theta+1)^2} = \frac{\theta}{(\theta+2)(\theta+1)^2} =0.03.\]

  \begin{enumerate}
  \def\labelenumii{(\alph{enumii})}
  \item
    Falso
